+/*
+ * Host-controller state sample (heartbeat v5). Boots 33/34 show the CPU stop
+ * inside the *second* UTRLDBR read of a completion poll, with the command in
+ * flight and every GCC clock branch still on. To catch a precursor, the 1 Hz
+ * thread records HCE/HCS/IS/UTRLDBR/UTRLRSR once a second. These are the same
+ * read-only HCI registers the driver itself polls; adding them here is the
+ * experiment: if hc_seq stops advancing at the failure instant, the MMIO read
+ * itself is what dies; if it keeps advancing, the controller is alive and only
+ * the driver's own path is stuck.
